cities\r\n   * Indian vehicle registration numbers such as UP14 AB 1234\r\n   * Masked Indian phone numbers such as 98XXXXXX21\r\n   * Indian rupee values such as ₹45,000\r\n\r\n4. Simplify the dashboard:\r\n\r\n   * 12 Persons\r\n   * 8 Locations\r\n   * 15 Relat\n<truncated 1232 bytes>\n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Project Goal**: Adapt and simplify the existing frontend prototype of **NEXUS** (AI-powered criminal network analysis system) for a **Smart India Hackathon (SIH)** presentation.\n- **Core Requirements**:\n  1. Replace US-style names with Indian sample names: *Rahul Verma*, *Amit Yadav*, *Priya Singh*, *Suresh Sharma*, *Neha Gupta* (and total 12 persons).\n  2. Replace US locations with Indian locations: *Delhi*, *Ghaziabad*, *Lucknow*, *Mirzapur*, *Noida* (and total 8 locations).\n  3. Use Indian-style data: vehicle plates (`UP14 AB 1234`, `DL01 CA 9988`), masked phone numbers (`+91 98XXXXXX21`, `+91 97XXXXXX45`), and rupee values (`₹45,000`, `₹12,50,000`).\n  4. Simplify Dashboard stats: exactly **12 Persons**, **8 Locations**, **15 Relationships**, **3 Possible Patterns**.\n  5. Simplify Network Graph: show **5–8 connected core entities** initially with prominent, readable labels suitable for hackathon judges.\n  6. Focus navigation on **5 main screens**:\n     - *Dashboard* (`/`)\n     - *Upload Evidence* (`/upload`)\n     - *Network Analysis* (`/network`)\n     - *Person Details* (`/person/:id`)\n     - *Evidence Details* (`/evidence/:id`)\n  7. Remove/hide advanced clutter (blockchain, crypto mixers, complex prediction, live police feeds).\n  8. Keep frontend modular and ready for future backend integration; do NOT build a backend or AI API yet.\n  9. Preserved existing React/Vite/TypeScript/Tailwind architecture without rebuilding from scratch.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Files Modified / Updated**:\n  - `src/data/mockData.ts`: Completely updated with 12 Indian persons, 8 locations, 15 relationships, 3 crime patterns (Hawala Loop, FASTag Transit, SIM Call Burst), Indian vehicles, masked phone numbers, and INR (`₹`) figures.\n  - `src/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx`: Simplified to the 5 requested main screens with *Special Cell // Delhi Police (SIH 2026)* branding.\n  - `src/components/layout/TopNav.tsx`: Updated with Indian Police metadata, search across Indian suspects, vehicle numbers (`UP14 AB 1234`), and phone numbers (`98XXXXXX21`).\n  - `src/components/network/NetworkGraphContainer.tsx`: Simplified to present 7 core nodes by default (Rahul Verma, Amit Yadav, Priya Singh, Suresh Sharma, Neha Gupta, Scorpio `UP14 AB 1234`, Canara Bank Hawala Acct) with readable labels, edge badges (`₹12.5L`), and an expandable toggle for live pitching.\n  - `src/pages/DashboardPage.tsx`: Overhauled to showcase the 4 exact KPI metrics, 3 detected crime patterns cards, mini topology radar, and suspects table.\n  - `src/pages/UploadEvidencePage.tsx`: Adapted for Indian evidence ingestion (CDR Telecom dump, FASTag ANPR photo hit, Canara Bank Hawala statement in ₹) with Section 65B compliance notes.\n  - `src/pages/EntityProfilePage.tsx`: Tailored as *Person Details* for Indian suspects with masked phones, vehicles, Indian IPC/PMLA charges, and ₹ transaction logs.\n  - `src/pages/EvidenceDetailsPage.tsx`: Newly created dedicated screen to inspect individual evidence files, Indian custodial officers (Sub-Insp R. K. Sharma), and Section 65B SHA-256 hashes.\n  - `src/pages/NetworkAnalysisPage.tsx`: Streamlined graph analysis workbench with a 1-click shortest link tracer (Rahul Verma ➔ Amit Yadav ➔ Hawala Bank Acct).\n  - `src/pages/LoginPage.tsx`: Updated with Delhi Police / UP STF department selections and one-click demo credentials.\n  - `src/components/common/AlertCard.tsx`: Updated to handle new Indian alert sources (`CDR CLUSTER`, `FASTag ANPR`, `BANK / UPI FLAGGED`, `AI PATTERN ENGINE`).\n  - `src/App.tsx`: Configured routing for `/`, `/upload`, `/network`, `/person/:id`, `/person`, `/evidence/:id`, `/evidence`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Fixes\n- **Syntax error in `src/types/index.ts` line 125**:\n  - While adding `EventCategory` and `TimelineEvent`, the closing curly brace `}` for `interface Evidence` was accidentally replaced or merged with line 125, causing: `TS1131: Property or signature expected`.\n  - Fix needed: Ensure `Evidence` interface ends properly with `}` on line 124 before `export type EventCategory = ...`.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- **Workspace Path**: `C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\nexus`\n- **TypeScript Config**: `tsconfig.app.json` has `paths: { \"@/*\": [\"./src/*\"] }`, `verbatimModuleSyntax: false`, and `noUnusedLocals: false`.\n- **Server Status**: Prior dev server task (`task-199`) was cancelled when user sent new message. Needs to be re-run after the syntax fix.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Next Steps (Priority Order)\n1. **Fix syntax in `src/types/index.ts`**:\n   - Insert the missing closing brace `}` on the `Evidence` interface right before `export type EventCategory`.\n2. **Run build verification**:\n   - Execute `npm run build` in `C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\nexus`. Ensure `tsc -b` and `vite build` complete with 0 errors.\n3. **Launch the development server**:\n   - Run `npm run dev -- --host --port 5173` as a background daemon (`IsDaemon: true`).\n4. **Verify all 5 main routes via HTTP**:\n   - Test `GET /` (Dashboard)\n   - Test `GET /upload` (Upload Evidence)\n   - Test `GET /network` (Network Analysis)\n   - Test `GET /person/ent-1` (Person Details)\n   - Test `GET /evidence/ev-1` (Evidence Details)\n5. **Update Walkthrough Artifact & Report to User**:\n   - Summarize the simplification and provide access URLs (`http://localhost:5173/` and LAN IP).\n\n---\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Do not rebuild the project from scratch**: Modify existing files in place.\n- **Do not add a backend or external AI APIs**: Keep everything in clean, reusable mock data files and modular