{"step_index":313,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-07T19:43:48Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-08T01:13:48+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-08T01:13:48+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/brain/fb69bf55-26d8-4420-a8a5-e461b2943c07/walkthrough.md`\nTotal Lines: 127\nTotal Bytes: 8633\nShowing lines 1 to 127\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # NEXUS // Criminal Network Analysis Intelligence Dashboard\n2: \n3: NEXUS is an AI-powered criminal network analysis frontend designed for law enforcement and intelligence task forces. Built with React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, React Router, and tactical UI primitives inspired by Palantir Gotham, Analyst's Notebook, and Maltego.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## Workspace Location\n8: The complete frontend project has been created and verified at:\n9: `C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\nexus`\n10: \n11: ---\n12: \n13: ## Key Features & Completed Pages\n14: \n15: ### 1. Login (`/login`)\n16: - **Law-Enforcement Gate**: Title 18 U.S.C. § 1030 warning header with real-time AES-256 link status.\n17: - **Officer Credentials**: Badge ID (`FED-8491`), encrypted hardware token PIN, and division selector (Transnational Crime, Cyber Warfare, Anti-Money Laundering, INTERPOL).\n18: - **Biometric Simulation**: Live hardware token validation sequence.\n19: - **Evaluation Profiles**: One-click quick-login triggers for \"Lead Investigator Sarah Vance\" and \"SIGINT Analyst\".\n20: \n21: ### 2. Dashboard (`/`)\n22: - **Command Center Telemetry**: Real-time status indicators with DEFCON-3 alert badge and sector telemetry.\n23: - **Tactical KPI Metric Cards**:\n24:   - *Active High-Value Targets* (42 HVTs with sparkline)\n25:   - *Tracked Illicit Financial Flow* ($148.6M across 16 jurisdictions)\n26:   - *Live Intercept Feeds* (189 active feeds)\n27:   - *AI Anomaly Threat Index* (84.2 with neural recalculation)\n28: - **Embedded Network Topology Radar**: Live interactive canvas showing the active criminal syndicate cluster for *Operation Phantom Web*.\n29: - **Priority Intercept Stream**: Triage alert feed with AI confidence metrics, source identifiers (SIGINT, FINCEN, ANPR), and plot actions.\n30: - **Active Operations Table**: Multi-jurisdictional case table with sorting, search, and status pills.\n31: \n32: ### 3. Cases & Warrants (`/cases`)\n33: - **Case Management**: Filter by status (*Active Investigation*, *Interdiction Imminent*, *Surveillance Phase*, *Grand Jury*) and priority (*CRITICAL*, *HIGH*, *MEDIUM*).\n34: - **Operational Metrics**: Aggregated warrants issued, seized asset values ($123.5M), and active target counts.\n35: - **Case Dossier Inspection**: Detailed drawer showing case charters, lead agents, jurisdiction, and linked suspects.\n36: - **Interactive Charter Issuance**: Modal to launch new operations with tactical codenames and AI auto-tagging.\n37: \n38: ### 4. Upload Evidence (`/upload`)\n39: - **Ingestion Vault**: Multi-format support for Call Detail Records (CDR), SWIFT wire ledgers, VoLTE audio intercepts, ANPR video, and forensic disk images.\n40: - **Automated SHA-256 Hashing**: Generates Title 18 compliant immutable checksums with instant clipboard copy.\n41: - **Chain of Custody Protocol**: Custodial officer name, badge number, and GPS collection location.\n42: - **4-Stage AI Pipeline Visualizer**:\n43:   1. *SHA-256 Checksum Verification*\n44:   2. *Named Entity Recognition (NER)*\n45:   3. *Biometric & Voiceprint Matching*\n46:   4. *Topology Graph Vectorization*\n47: - **Verified Archive Binder**: Live cards showing ingested items with inspection modals for raw intercept payloads.\n48: \n49: ### 5. Network Analysis Workbench (`/network`)\n50: - **Full-Screen Interactive Topology**:\n51:   - Zoom in/out, pan, reset view, and zoom percentage indicator.\n52:   - Multi-node classification: Suspects (red), Shell Companies (amber), Burner Phones (cyan), Bank Accounts (emerald), Safehouses (purple), Vehicles (sky blue).\n53:   - Relationship vectors: Wire transfers with money pill badges, encrypted VoLTE calls (dashed), co-conspirators, and courier links.\n54:   - Filter Drawer: Threat score slider (0-95+), entity class toggles, and suspicious transfer highlights.\n55:   - Node Inspector Drawer: Degree centrality, betweenness score, legal status, direct vectors, and one-click pivot to full dossier.\n56:   - **Shortest Attribution Pathfinder**: Calculates shortest network path between targets (e.g. Viktor Ramos ➔ Elena Rostova ➔ Aethelgard Holdings ➔ Zurich Credit Union).\n57:   - Graph export options (JSON, Gephi bundle).\n58: \n59: ### 6. Entity Profile Dossier (`/entity/:id`)\n60: - **Target Intelligence Dossier**:\n61:   - High-Value Target header with tactical photo/mugshot, wanted charges, calculated threat index (e.g. 96/100), and last known GPS coordinates with timestamp.\n62:   - Quick target switcher strip to jump between syndicate members.\n63:   - Tabbed intelligence views:\n64:     - *Overview*: Biographical data, aliases, weapons, biometrics, active charges.\n65:     - *Network Associates*: Direct co-conspirators with connection weights and risk ratings.\n66:     - *Financial Footprint*: Structured offshore wires and layering breakdown.\n67:     - *Intercepted Comms*: Transcribed Title-III intercepts and VoLTE recordings.\n68:     - *Evidence Vault*: Directly linked cryptographic evidence items.\n69:     - *AI Threat Evaluation*: LLM synthesis of flight risk (92.4%), asset dissipation risk, and tactical interdiction recommendations.\n70: \n71: ### 7. Investigation Timeline (`/timeline`)\n72: - **Chronological Intelligence Stream**: Chronological event correlation with custom icon bullets for wiretaps, financial transfers, border crossings, raids, and comms.\n73: - **Filter Controls**: Filter by event category and target entity correlation.\n74: - **Corroboration Confidence**: AI confidence rating on each timeline event with direct links to cryptographic evidence references.\n75: - **Event Inspection Modal**: Drill down into event context, participants, and timestamp data.\n76: \n77: ### 8. System Settings (`/settings`)\n78: - **AI Neural Parameters**:\n79:   - Financial anomaly sensitivity slider\n80:   - Facial recognition match confidence slider\n81:   - Autonomous graph edge creation toggle\n82:   - Voiceprint acoustic clustering toggle\n83: - **Interface & Themes**:\n84:   - One-click toggle between Tactical Dark Mode and Analytical Light Mode.\n85:   - Data density toggles and classification watermarking.\n86: - **Officer Credentials & Security**:\n87:   - FIDO2 hardware token status, clearance level (Level 5 Alpha), and session countdown.\n88: - **CJIS Audit Log**:\n89:   - Immutable activity log with timestamped entries and SHA-256 signatures.\n90: \n91: ---\n92: \n93: ## Reusable Components Implemented\n94: \n95: | Component | Path | Description |\n96: | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n97: | **Sidebar** | [Sidebar.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx) | Collapsible tactical sidebar with classification badge, active mission pill, and live route counters |\n98: | **TopNav** | [TopNav.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/layout/TopNav.tsx) | Global intelligence search, classification banner, theme toggle, and alert dropdown |\n99: | **MetricCard** | [MetricCard.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/common/MetricCard.tsx) | KPI cards with dynamic sparkline SVGs, trend indicators, and severity glow borders |\n100: | **DataTable** | [DataTable.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/common/DataTable.tsx) | Generic sortable, searchable, paginated tactical table component |\n101: | **NetworkGraphContainer** | [NetworkGraphContainer.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/network/NetworkGraphContainer.tsx) | Interactive SVG network graph with pan, zoom, node selection, edge labeling, and filtering |\n102: | **EvidenceCard** | [EvidenceCard.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/common/EvidenceCard.tsx) | Evidence cards with SHA-256 copy, file format badges, and raw intercept modal |\n103: | **EntityCard** | [EntityCard.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/common/EntityCard.tsx) | Suspect cards with threat gauge, aliases, GPS location, and graph plot actions |\n104: | **AlertCard** | [AlertCard.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/common/AlertCard.tsx) | Operational alert cards with AI confidence meter, source tag, and triage actions |\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: ## Verification Results\n109: \n110: ### Build Verification\n111: - Executed `npm run build`:\n112:   - `tsc -b` passed with 0 errors.\n113:   - `vite build` completed in **788ms**.\n114:   - Generated assets: `dist/index.html` (1.28 kB), `dist/assets/index.css` (37.84 kB), `dist/assets/index.js` (421.70 kB).\n115: \n116: ### Live Server & Route HTTP Verification\n117: - Vite development server started at `http://localhost:5173/`.\n118: - Tested all 8 routes via automated HTTP requests:\n119:   - `GET /` ➔ **200 OK**\n120:   - `GET /login` ➔ **200 OK**\n121:   - `GET /cases` ➔ **200 OK**\n122:   - `GET /upload` ➔ **200 OK**\n123:   - `GET /network` ➔ **200 OK**\n124:   - `GET /entity/ent-1` ➔ **200 OK**\n125:   - `GET /timeline` ➔ **200 OK**\n126:   - `GET /settings` ➔ **200 OK**\n127: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":314,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-07T19:43:48Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Detailed summary of the simplified NEXUS frontend prototype adapted for Smart India Hackathon (SIH), featuring Indian law enforcement sample data (Delhi Police, UP STF), 5 streamlined screens, 12 persons, 8 locations, 15 relationships, 3 AI crime patterns, and a 5-8 node high-visibility network graph.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# NEXUS // AI-Powered Criminal Network Analysis Dashboard\n### Smart India Hackathon (SIH 2026) Frontend Prototype\n\nThe NEXUS frontend has been streamlined and tailored for an **Indian law-enforcement context** (Special Cell Delhi Police & Uttar Pradesh Special Task Force - UP STF) for competition pitching and live judge demonstrations.\n\n---\n\n## 📍 Workspace & Server Access\n- **Workspace Directory**: `C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\nexus`\n- **Local URL**: [http://localhost:5173/](http://localhost:5173/)\n- **Network / LAN URL**: `http://10.11.2.57:5173/`\n- **Build Status**: Production build passed cleanly with 0 TypeScript errors (`tsc -b && vite build`).\n\n---\n\n## 🇮🇳 Indian Law-Enforcement Data Implemented\n\n### 1. Sample Suspects & Persons (12 Total)\n* **Core 5 Suspects**:\n  1. **Rahul Verma** (Kingpin / Hawala Operator, Delhi Chandni Chowk, High Threat 94/100)\n  2. **Amit Yadav** (Enforcer & Logistics, Ghaziabad Indirapuram, Threat 88/100)\n  3. **Priya Singh** (Financial Mule / Shell Firms, Lucknow Hazratganj, Threat 79/100)\n  4. **Suresh Sharma** (Weapons & Cross-Border Logistics, Mirzapur, Threat 85/100)\n  5. **Neha Gupta** (Tech & VoIP Facilitator, Noida Sector 62, Threat 72/100)\n* **Additional 7 Persons**:\n  6. **Vikram Malhotra** (Noida Sector 18)\n  7. **Deepak Rawat** (Meerut Cantt)\n  8. **Sunita Devi** (Kanpur Nagar)\n  9. **Manoj Tiwari** (Varanasi Cantt)\n  10. **Anjali Kashyap** (Ghaziabad Raj Nagar)\n  11. **Harish Chandra** (Delhi Rohini)\n  12. **Pooja Saxena** (Lucknow Gomti Nagar)\n\n### 2. Sample Locations (8 Core Monitored Corridors)\n1. **Delhi** (Chandni Chowk / Connaught Place / Rohini)\n2. **Ghaziabad** (Indirapuram / Raj Nagar)\n3. **Lucknow** (Hazratganj / Gomti Nagar)\n4. **Mirzapur** (Chunar / Rural Corridor)\n5. **Noida** (Sector 62 / Sector 18)\n6. **Meerut** (Cantt / Transport Nagar)\n7. **Kanpur** (Civil Lines / Transport Hub)\n8. **Varanasi** (Cantt Station Area)\n\n### 3. Realistic Indian Identifiers & Evidence\n- **Indian Vehicle Plates**: `UP14 AB 1234` (Mahindra Scorpio), `DL01 CA 9988` (Toyota Fortuner), `UP32 EK 4411`, `DL04 BK 5520`, etc.\n- **Masked Phone Numbers**: `+91 98XXXXXX21`, `+91 97XXXXXX45`, `+91 99XXXXXX10`, `+91 98XXXXXX88`, `+91 96XXXXXX33`, etc.\n- **Indian Rupee Figures**: `₹45,000`, `₹12,50,000`, `₹4,20,000`, `₹8,90,000`, `₹25,00,000`, etc.\n- **Statutory Compliance**: Indian Evidence Act Section 65B electronic certificate compliance, SHA-256 integrity hashes, IPC/BNS charges (Section 120B, 420, 384, Arms Act 25, PMLA 3/4).\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 4 Core Dashboard KPI Metrics\n1. **Tracked Persons**: **12 Persons** (5 High-Value Targets, 7 active associates)\n2. **Monitored Locations**: **8 Locations** (NCR & UP Corridors: Delhi, Ghaziabad, Lucknow, Mirzapur, Noida, etc.)\n3. **Identified Connections**: **15 Relationships** (Direct calls, Hawala wires, vehicle registrations)\n4. **AI Detected Modus**: **3 Possible Patterns** (Hawala Loop, FASTag Transit, Call Burst)\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ 3 Detected Crime Patterns (Modus Operandi)\n1. **Hawala Fund Layering Loop**: Circular transfer of ₹12,50,000 originating from a Chandni Chowk bullion trader, routed through Amit Yadav in Ghaziabad, and deposited into Priya Singh shell accounts in Lucknow within 4 hours.\n2. **FASTag Toll Corridor Transit**: Mahindra Scorpio (`UP14 AB 1234`) clocked crossing Chhijarsi Toll Plaza (NH-9) at 02:14 AM and Jewar Toll Plaza at 03:22 AM, matching CDR cell-tower tower dump of Suresh Sharma.\n3. **Burner SIM Call Burst (Pre-Crime)**: Coordinated burst of 38 short-duration VoLTE calls (<45s) across 3 masked burner SIMs (`98XXXXXX21` ➔ `97XXXXXX45`) immediately preceding cash transit.\n\n---\n\n## 🧭 Simplified 5 Main Screens\n\n| Route | Page | Key Features for Hackathon Pitch |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `/` | **Dashboard** | 4 clean KPI cards, 3 AI Modus Operandi pattern cards, embedded network radar, recent Indian alerts feed, and 12 tracked suspects table. |\n| `/upload` | **Upload Evidence** | CDR telecom dumps, FASTag ANPR toll camera logs, Canara Bank Hawala statements with Indian Section 65B certificate notes, SHA-256 hash generator, and 4-step AI pipeline visualizer. |\n| `/network` | **Network Analysis** | Interactive SVG graph showing **5 to 8 connected core entities** by default with prominent readable labels, edge badges (e.g. ₹12.5L Hawala), 1-click shortest link tracer (Rahul Verma ➔ Amit Yadav ➔ Hawala Bank Acct), and toggle to expand to all 15 syndicate nodes. |\n| `/person/:id` | **Person Details** | Detailed suspect dossier: photo, calculated threat score, alias, masked mobile, vehicle registration, Indian IPC/PMLA charges, bank footprint in ₹, and CDR call history. |\n| `/evidence/:id` | **Evidence Details** | Single evidence inspector: Section 65B compliance verification, custodial officer (Sub-Insp R. K. Sharma), SHA-256 verification badge, linked suspects, and raw extracted payload. |\n\n---\n\n## 🕸️ High-Visibility Network Graph (5 to 8 Core Entities)\nTo prevent overwhelming hackathon judges:\n- **Default Core Mode (7 prominent nodes)**:\n  1. `Rahul Verma` (Suspect, Red Badge)\n  2. `Amit Yadav` (Suspect, Red Badge)\n  3. `Priya Singh` (Suspect, Red Badge)\n  4. `Suresh Sharma` (Suspect, Red Badge)\n  5. `Neha Gupta` (Suspect, Red Badge)\n  6. `Scorpio [UP14 AB 1234]` (Vehicle, Cyan Badge)\n  7. `Canara Bank [Hawala Acct]` (Financial, Emerald Badge)\n- **Edge Badges**: Bold labels such as `₹12.5L Hawala`, `₹4.2L Layering`, `Vehicle Registered`, `38 Calls Burst`.\n- **Expandable**: One-click *\"Show All 15 Nodes\"* toggle available during technical Q&A with judges.\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Future Backend Architecture Readiness\nThe frontend remains strictly decoupled from backend services, making it prepared for future integration:\n- All data models reside in clean TypeScript interfaces ([types/index.ts](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/types/index.ts)).\n- Mock databases and relations are isolated in [mockData.ts](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/data/mockData.ts).\n- Ready to be swapped with REST API or FastAPI / Django / Node.js backend endpoints without frontend refactoring.\n","Description":"Update walkthrough artifact with Indian SIH hackathon specifications and live server status","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\fb69bf55-26d8-4420-a8a5-e461b2943c07\\walkthrough.md","toolAction":"Writing walkthrough.md","toolSummary":"Update walkthrough.md with SIH features and Indian data"}}]}
